      "text": "$\\left|\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3 i}{8}\\right| = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(-\\frac{3}{8}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{4}{8}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{3}{8}\\right)^2} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{8}}.$\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(1 cm);\n\ndraw((-1,-1)--(1,-1),linewidth(1.2));\ndraw((2,0)--(2,-1)--(3,-1),linewidth(1.2));\ndraw((-1.5,1)--(1.5,1),linewidth(1.2));\ndraw((-1.5,-1)--(1.5,-1),linewidth(1.2));\n\ndot((-1,-1));\ndot((1,-1));\ndot((2,0));\ndot((3,0));\ndot((2,-1));\ndot((2,1));\n\nlabel(\"$2$\", (2,-1), E);\n[/asy] We can estimate the answer using a guess and check method.\nWe see that $\\frac{1}{2}$ is closer to 0 than $\\frac{3}{8}$, so we guess that $\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i$ is farther from 0 than $\\frac{3}{8}i$. We can confirm this by evaluating $| \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i|$ and comparing it to $|\\frac{3}{8}i|$.\nBy the Pythagorean Theorem, $\\left|\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i\\right| = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{9}{64}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{73}{64}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{8}$. However, since $\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i$ is actually deeper in the lower half plane, it is farther from 0 than $\\frac{1}{2}$. Therefore, $\\left|\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i\\right| < \\frac{1}{2} = |6i|$. Thus, $\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{8}} = \\frac{5}{8}$. The answer is: \\frac{5}{8}",
