      "text": "To evaluate the magnitude (or absolute value) of a complex number \\(a + bi\\), we use the formula:\n\n\\[\n|a + bi| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\n\\]\n\nGiven our problem, we need to find the magnitude of the complex number \\(\\frac 12 - \\frac 38 i\\). This corresponds to \\(a = \\frac 12\\) and \\(b = -\\frac 38\\).\n\nSubstitute \\(a = \\frac 12\\) and \\(b = -\\frac 38\\):\n\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac 12 - \\frac 38 i \\right| = \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac 12 \\right)^2 + \\left( -\\frac 38 \\right)^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) ^2 + \\left(\\frac{3}{8}\\right)^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{9}{64}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{64} + \\frac{9}{64}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{64}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{5}{8}\n\\]\n\nThus, the magnitude (or absolute value) of the complex number \\(\\frac 12 - \\frac 38 i\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{5}{8}}\n\\]",
